        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4e601fd8-929a-3946-875d-4e87dde48afa",
                "word": "geloei",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                        "entry_id": "4e601fd8-929a-3946-875d-4e87dde48afa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "het aanhoudend een luid geluid maken dat lijkt op dat van een koe"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d31b820a-e85f-4315-84a0-abd09785e641",
                                "sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                                "text": "Een verslaggever van ITV, die als een van de eersten ter plaatse was, zag een man zijn echtgenote ondersteunen. ,,Toen ze zich omdraaide, schrok ik me rot: haar shirt was rood van het bloed.” Druppelsgewijs kwamen meer van zulke gruwelijke details naar buiten. Het onafgebroken geloei van sirenes maakte de sfeer grimmig."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3a328d7-c752-4022-824c-d42cf9745c00",
                                "sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                                "text": "Dawson Tamatea werkte bijna dertig jaar op de Palmerton North Boys High School in Nieuw-Zeeland. Hij gaf onder andere lichamelijke opvoeding en wiskunde. Op de video is te zien hoe duizenden scholieren in uniform vol overgave de haka uitvoeren voor hun geliefde leraar. Zodra de dans is afgelopen passeert de lijkwagen de groep. Het geloei en geschreeuw van de scholieren maken plaats voor een doodse stilte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2dcd245-fac5-49f4-a5ed-6892bd4badf1",
                                "sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                                "text": "Door de boxen nog steeds het hartverscheurende geloei. De baby is een ongewenst bijproduct dat straks als lap vlees in het koelvak van de supermarkt ligt. Het koelvak naast de zuivelsectie waar de melk in pakken wordt verkocht. Melk dat eigenlijk bedoeld was voor hem…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f651ff51-0508-466c-880c-94c32d7f1433",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e601fd8-929a-3946-875d-4e87dde48afa",
                        "source_sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                        "target_lang_word": "howling of wind",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c5ef234-4ffb-4457-944e-7c37be505e13",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e601fd8-929a-3946-875d-4e87dde48afa",
                        "source_sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                        "target_lang_word": "howling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "howling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c09c10a2-be6e-3896-aa94-e856bb90e8d9",
                                        "entry_id": "7c4f5d1a-0e75-32e9-8f0a-7c92250b760b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of producing howls."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a64ec11-9488-4743-8727-a8237abe6803",
                                                "sense_id": "c09c10a2-be6e-3896-aa94-e856bb90e8d9",
                                                "text": "The howling of wolves is haunting at night."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "howling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81478a67-3427-379b-b774-40dd4aed75b7",
                                        "entry_id": "92748fa0-df34-3f73-bc52-147eba011eb4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of howl"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e59af311-12d2-478b-bb92-c6f4418baa45",
                                                "sense_id": "81478a67-3427-379b-b774-40dd4aed75b7",
                                                "text": "\"They have turned a great old English institution into a shameful clip-joint. It's a shuddering, howling tragedy.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "howling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eebdc196-e22e-348b-9c25-ee62fa555875",
                                        "entry_id": "c43e11dd-a6c4-32d4-999e-f5f48cd89105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That howls."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b210467f-e9ae-482e-9cb8-6c7d9e3b65a3",
                                                "sense_id": "eebdc196-e22e-348b-9c25-ee62fa555875",
                                                "text": "A few minutes later a howling mob was at the door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fbdcb32-517f-4bd1-88ac-14b211a85ca7",
                                                "sense_id": "eebdc196-e22e-348b-9c25-ee62fa555875",
                                                "text": "We have already seen in Chapter I how man stepped upwards from the level of a howling brute to the higher level of an articulate being, and thence to the still higher level of a singing creature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc577c6-511e-4066-a176-5dedbb8a1174",
                                                "sense_id": "eebdc196-e22e-348b-9c25-ee62fa555875",
                                                "text": "It consisted of marching on to College green or St Stephen's green on a day when there was a howling gale and the wind was blowing about us –I am sure hon. Members today are familiar with this –to utter a few, well-chosen platitudes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f58794ef-9f93-396b-8f0a-a30be0ab41b9",
                                        "entry_id": "c43e11dd-a6c4-32d4-999e-f5f48cd89105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That causes one to howl or feel like howling; deeply distressing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a77b47e9-5782-4328-a868-e94d45ca022d",
                                                "sense_id": "f58794ef-9f93-396b-8f0a-a30be0ab41b9",
                                                "text": "Ah! the death of the poor, the empty entrails, howling hunger, the animal appetite that leads one with chattering teeth to fill one's stomach with beastly refuse in this great Paris, so bright and golden!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe6eeb90-ed97-4405-b3c0-33317129dd0f",
                                                "sense_id": "f58794ef-9f93-396b-8f0a-a30be0ab41b9",
                                                "text": "Some agency must control the allocation of frequencies or all our airways would be a howling chaos: but there is no rational justification for the kind of regulation that the Federal Communications Commission proposes for our industry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7af5e9e0-60ac-470d-8b82-63621e856866",
                                                "sense_id": "f58794ef-9f93-396b-8f0a-a30be0ab41b9",
                                                "text": "A pervasive sense of optimism led settlers in southern New Zealand to transform their properites from a 'howling wilderness' to a humanised rural landscape."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54bc95cb-31aa-3d67-af06-6f55c3adfa16",
                                        "entry_id": "c43e11dd-a6c4-32d4-999e-f5f48cd89105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used as an intensifier"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcd3a257-db10-46d9-948f-7011c4345e6f",
                                                "sense_id": "54bc95cb-31aa-3d67-af06-6f55c3adfa16",
                                                "text": "Those were days that I had success, for I could see it, and feel it, and taste it, and my patrons caught the contagion and we had a howling success ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f8b7328-9bbd-45e6-a994-5e0d0013d4d3",
                                                "sense_id": "54bc95cb-31aa-3d67-af06-6f55c3adfa16",
                                                "text": "Boy, what a howling triumph if we should find our way out of here and go walking into Stark House by night !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27326293-d82d-4d4d-b3a3-d0056243b9ce",
                                                "sense_id": "54bc95cb-31aa-3d67-af06-6f55c3adfa16",
                                                "text": "The majority of your audience comes to your tale with one hopeful expectation: Tell me a howling good story."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c3274ae-99f9-45e5-998b-d9c208e0ac58",
                                                "sense_id": "54bc95cb-31aa-3d67-af06-6f55c3adfa16",
                                                "text": "a howling success"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "194a110f-4a86-4c37-9e2d-0c268527dcc7",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e601fd8-929a-3946-875d-4e87dde48afa",
                        "source_sense_id": "92ae18a9-5d74-3fb0-ae96-cd35e2022076",
                        "target_lang_word": "roaring",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "roaring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1e8e5dd-fabc-3f81-8fd5-bfcd15c47a23",
                                        "entry_id": "357a46fe-98c8-338b-82b4-a10a1fb9260f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intensive; extreme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdc89bf8-b73a-406a-8921-92c699fac3ff",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e8e5dd-fabc-3f81-8fd5-bfcd15c47a23",
                                                "text": "“[…] the awfully hearty sort of Christmas cards that people do send to other people that they don't know at all well. You know. The kind that have mottoes like\n Here's rattling good luck and roaring good cheer, / With lashings of food and great hogsheads of beer. […]”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11ef36fe-bae6-3240-897d-fa03e2d31fb9",
                                        "entry_id": "357a46fe-98c8-338b-82b4-a10a1fb9260f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very successful; lively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56ebf8f8-e8e1-4dfe-a993-d3f2f1b40ed2",
                                                "sense_id": "11ef36fe-bae6-3240-897d-fa03e2d31fb9",
                                                "text": "The ice-cream sellers did a roaring trade in the midday heat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae841cde-07fb-4a5c-87bf-9eb0038d235b",
                                                "sense_id": "11ef36fe-bae6-3240-897d-fa03e2d31fb9",
                                                "text": "But finally we came to a river with hundreds of boats upon it, and there was a magnificent bridge, and on the other bank was a roaring city, and through the fog the rain came down thick as the tears of the angels. \"That 's London,\" said I."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd28f51b-aa38-4b86-be2c-b8f9b19a8d37",
                                                "sense_id": "11ef36fe-bae6-3240-897d-fa03e2d31fb9",
                                                "text": "Some of the worst offenders were rounded up and sent home as Rozhestvensky's health began to recover. But this further diminished the fleet's manpower. And, at the same time, many of the officers were quite-happily unaware that anything was going on, having discovered that Madagascar did a roaring trade in various high-strength drugs. One officer had brought^([sic – meaning bought?]) 2,000 cigarettes, and they were found to all be filled with opium, much to the joy of all those who could get their hands on them before they were confiscated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "roaring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6731340-f837-3b5b-98ec-baf81540cef8",
                                        "entry_id": "114a9dfa-b178-3abe-9f48-fa81f7221582",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of roar"
                                        ],
